A||N||36||grinthock||Multimedia Fiero's - My Project...||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||05-31-2001||08:34 PM||||Ok everyone --- I hope to have this done by Michigan, it's gonna take alot of time, and I dunno how pretty it's gonna look but I am in the process of building something for my fiero.....<P>This will be totally custom, I am building it from the ground up....<P>The 1.5 DIN area will be replaced with a 6.5" LCD Screen.<P>Mounted (somewhere, still deciding!) will be a on board Pentium III computer system.  This, with the custom software I am developing right now will give the ability to display the following and perform these functions<P>- Monitor all the fiero's internal sensors, and ECM readouts (use's Oliver's Hardware!)<P>- Provide audible alerts on vehicle conditions, including codes, and display their TEXT<P>- Play MP3's to my hearts delight<P>- Play DVD Movies, Video CD's, MPG, AVI and off-the-air TV<P>- Provide a GPS based on-board navigation sytstem, with voice guidance<P>- Voice Activated Control (this is gonna require alot of work, this will probably be WAY later in the project)<P>- AM/FM Radio WITH RDS/ID Logic and recording capabilities, with upto 500 presets in 100 groups<P>- Voice Memo<P>- IR Remote Control<P>- Rear View and Front View Cameras for recording purposes, IE recording track runs, or driving inthe city.  These Cams' will be adaptable, could be placed anywhere I want (custom mounts being built)<P>- Onboard Screen Saver and slideshow (Photo's provided by BanditBalz FIEROCD)<P>- Custom Menu's built, all setup with the Pontiac FIERO Theme.<P>- Built in Security Alarm<P>There are so many possibilities here, I am sure there are more items I havn't thought of yet, these are the ones I have figured through and decided I am working on, to make it easy for car use I need to write custom software so it is basic point and click.  <P>It's a project that I see as VERY easily attainable, and low cost.  I figure the cost to come under $1500 Canadian (1000 USD), using some parts I have sitting around here.<P>I will let everyone know when it's done, progress WILL be available (Not yet so don't flood the site lookin K?) on my web site <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A> <P>When I have started......  Screenshots will be available as soon as I get down to writing the interface, right now, the interface is far from my mind, i need function before beauty, anyone with questions, ideas or comments POST THEM!  I want to make this great....<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://grinthock.2y.net/pics/87gt/S_P000386.JPG">    <P>Home page: <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroworld.com</A> <P>Owner of 85 GT<BR>87 GT Silver<BR>1995 Ford Escort Wagoon POS<P>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 05-31-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroHeather||05-31-2001||08:41 PM||||What do you need a computer that is beautiful for?  You've got me as your passenger  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  LOL||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||05-31-2001||10:02 PM||||That's one heck of an idea!  I bet you could do it though.  Cameras could be hidden under or next to the front and rear license plates.<P>Configuring an alarm system might be a little tough.  If you used an exisiting one though, as a seperate entity, you could make a screen flash though.  As in, hook up some sort of input to the computer that is triggered when the alarm is going off, have it play a "warning" Mp3 or something, and flash a message on the screen "You will die now..." hehehe.  You could also have similar things for the alarm's other functions, i.e. arm/disarm, trunk pop, etc.<P>IR control is definatly a must.  There isnt any "pretty" way that I can think of to mount a laptop and still have it easily accessed.  You could, however, have a little remote control to toggle between your modes (Mp3 player, Car scan (oliver's stuff), slideshow, movie, etc), and then have the laptop hidden under the pass side footwell.  You could even put it on drawer slides, so you (or your passenger) could pull it out, flip the top, and then change whatever you needed to.<P>If you have it done my the Michigan Show, you better look me up because I've got to see it!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||05-31-2001||11:08 PM||||It's definitely possible, and not really too complicated if you are good finding/tweaking software.  I talked with a few friends at school...get a few electrical, software, computer, and automotive engineers all in one room and you'd be amazed at the stuff we dream up <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I don't have any ingenius ideas for you right now...my brain has ceased functioning I've been working so much lately...but, make sure you draw out wiring schematics for everything, and keep track of how you did it.  I guarantee people will ask you for details, and it'd be way easier to post it on the web than to try to help them out one by one!  (This is also my non-mooch method of getting access to your R&D <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  I'll be at the Michigan show, hope to see your progress then!  Good luck, and make sure if you have something you're having a hard time with, to post it here.  There's a huge wealth of knowledge on just about anything if you ask!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-31-2001||11:16 PM||||You know I was sitting in my car the other day and dreamed up just that very same thing. You wouldnt happen to be the tall sultry brunett that offered to help rewire my circuts.... to ahh to install a computer to do exactly what you described..... are you? Or did she pay you a visit as well?||||reg||11
