Z||000030||Joe Torma||08-22-2001||10:13 PM||||Pictures?  And give it all away?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I'm kinda waiting for something to be fully completed...unless you want to see WIP pics.<P>As soon as I update the display drivers to capture video I'll have the car computer take its own pics. Win2000 is being a pain.<P>My setup is more "showy" than most.  All the car computers I've seen are just home computers sitting in the trunk.  I don't feel this is too creative. So I've integrated it into the front trunk.  Less weight than the spare tire, and more functional!  It has a fan controller that regulates the temp in the compartment when the computer is on.  I just need to get new weatherstripping on before final installation.  <P>My dash is holding me up too.  I've repositioned the guages and made things pretty swoopy.  It has more ideal speaker location(for the driver) for when I compete in IASCA SQ next year. The center section is angled twords me but the screen can swing twords the passenger. <P>I am keeping the head unit...the incredible new Premier unit ...I'll get a picture of my car downloaded into it soon.  If the tuner cards are anything like my home stereo it would suck...rotten reception.<P>Oh, anyone know how well those infarred cameras work??? Can we say night vision?!<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000031||Nashco||08-23-2001||02:04 AM||||I pray to god you're taking WIP pictures, those are the best ones!  I know you have a one-of-a-kind mod, but it's always nice to spread the wealth and show everybody how you did it.  I'd love to see what you've got so far!  I can't believe that so few people are interested in this; must be a lot of people that don't realize how much potential there is in an onboard computer....the possibilities are unlimited, especially with a fresh computer setup (usb, faster processing, high graphics capabilities, awesome multimedia systems, etc.)<P>How long have you had a Fiero Joe?  I am seeing you all over the place lately, and you're new from July...obviously you've had the car for a while now; isn't this forum awesome? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>P.S.  Grinthock...where did you end up hitting the big red HOLD button?  Halfway complete, more, less?  Do you have any pics?||||reg||1
Z||000032||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||08:07 AM||||Yeah, I just recently discovered/got addicted to the forum(read:now I spend way too much time here--especially when I should be sleeping).  This forum(and its members) is awesome!  Wish I could have met people at some shows this year.<P>I've had my Fiero for like 5 years.  I worked for Fiero Specialties for a few years so I know some stuff.  The only Fiero show I attended/showed at was Gettyburg 97...if anyone remembers, I had an amp rack a that moved to reveal the CD changer.<P>The computer does have a lot of potential and yes, I have WIP pics!   Lots of experimenting, as with my whole car.  I will let the cat further out of the bag, later.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Joe<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000033||MinnGreenGT||08-23-2001||09:44 AM||||Joe... send out some WIP pics- I'd love to see them!<P>Grinthock... sorry to hear your project is on hold. I've been thinking of doing a simple entertainment center in my GT.  A small LCD where the current map pocket is (directly in front of passenger seat) connected to an in-car tuner-vcr and/or DVD player.  Also throw in a new style PS1 (Sony's 2nd generation Playstation- about the size of a discman!) to play GT2 or similiar.  should be fairly easy- and the LCD screens are cheap on ebay. But most of my projects are on temporary hold until some funds show up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000034||Nashco||08-26-2001||05:01 AM||||Pics...insight...info...yes/no?  What are/were your major stumbling points?  What do you hope to integrate later?  Want to do something, but need suggestions as to how you should do it?  Any approximate costs for the items?<P>Just a few questions you might want to entertain...if you want, I could take this off list and not publicize your secrets <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Sent me a personal message if you want!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000035||KRMFiero||08-26-2001||10:53 AM||||I tryed doing that, but a 6.5" screen will not fit in the 1.5 din spot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   then try finding a safe spot for the computer <BR>- rear trunck; too hot <BR>- behind seat; seat will be to far foward <BR>- front trunk; big chance of getting wet<P>Get a laptop off e-bay with a brokin screen or something and use that for the actuall computer (put behind seat) a full computer (even with a small custom case) would be to big<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000036||Mach10||08-26-2001||01:12 PM||||I've been in the process of creating such a beast for the past year. It WAS going into my Mazda, but I broke that peice of junk on a brick wall. I'm waiting untill I have some cash to continue, but I've figured out a way of maybe having a full 800x600x32 HUD. It's going to take some work to fit, though...<BR>My method of controlling it was via a palm pilot wired to a built-in PC. I have a friend in CompSci that was going to help me work on the software. My project is in "snail" mode until I have the cash. I'm done "my" version of windows. (axed explorer, made my own shell controllable by mouse only) It's stable as hell, and I can use all of my hardware without pissing around looking for drivers like in Linux.<P>Linux IS a better platform, but ONLY if you like intensive coding. And making your own drivers. ||||reg||6
